  id: Descending_pectoral_muscle_Superficial_pectoral.L
  partName: Descending_pectoral_muscle_Superficial_pectoral.L
  descriptionChunks:
  - 'The descending pectoral muscle originates from the sternum and inserts into
    the forelimb, functioning primarily to draw the limb inward toward the body.
    It plays a key role in stabilizing the limb during standing and movement. '
  - Additionally, it helps control limb positioning during locomotion, preventing
    excessive outward motion. This muscle contributes to balance and coordinated
    movement, particularly during activities that require precision and control,
    ensuring smooth and efficient functioning of the forelimb.
